# Sealgate MCP server

This repo is the public MCP server for Sealgate, an AI data-leak-prevention
platform. The server is a thin MCP proxy: it forwards tool calls to an
Sealgate gateway, configured via SEALGATE_GATEWAY_URL and SEALGATE_API_KEY.
Sealgate runs managed release hosts (the remote MCP gateway at mcp.sealgate.ai,
advertised in the discovery manifests, and the Management API at
dashboard.sealgate.ai), but demo and self-hosted orgs run their own, so this
package stays host-agnostic: never hardcode a gateway URL or key.

## Stack
- Bun + TypeScript, MCP TypeScript SDK (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk), zod.
- Biome for lint/format: 4-space indent, double quotes.

## Layout
- src/index.ts      entrypoint (stdio by default, optional HTTP via env)
- src/server.ts     builds the McpServer and registers tools
- src/config.ts     validates the two env vars with zod
- src/gateway.ts    fetch wrapper that calls the Sealgate gateway with Bearer auth
- src/tools/        one file per proxy tool

## Working here
- Build: `bun run build`  (or `bunx tsc --noEmit` to typecheck)
- Test:  `bun test`
- All checks: `make ci`  (lint, deadcode, typecheck, tech-debt, duplicate-code,
  import boundaries, markdown links, AI-writing, Claude/Codex sync)
- Run the server: `bun run src/index.ts` (add `--help` for usage)
- No em dashes in any file; the AI-writing check fails on them.
- Tools must fail gracefully (return an error result) when the env is unset,
  never throw at startup.
